	abstract = {Summary This chapter aims to articulate a method for combining assessments of the individual components of sampling and nonsampling errors into a unified total survey error (TSE) distribution. It also aims to apply this method to derive TSE distributions for the National Immunization Survey (NIS), a large telephone survey in the U.S.A. of young children 19-35 months to monitor their vaccination statuses, conducted by the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC). The chapter describes TSE analysis for the 2012 NIS. Total error in this case relates to CDC's official 2012 vaccination coverage rates derived from provider-reported vaccination histories and final survey weights for the set of children deemed to have adequate provider data. When applied to vaccination coverage rates for sociodemographic domains, the analysis of TSE distributions reveals broad credible intervals and little evidence of differential total error.},
