	abstract = {Summary This chapter aims to make researchers, policy makers, and others aware of the difficulties related to survey research among ethnic minorities. Total survey error (TSE) provides a useful framework for understanding and discussing these difficulties, as well as the choices survey researchers face when designing studies of ethnic minorities and the consequences of these choices. The chapter looks at cost-related considerations in connection to survey design choices and their effect on the quality of data collected among ethnic minorities. Difficulties regarding the representation and the measurement of ethnic minorities arise both in surveys targeting ethnic minorities and in surveys of the general population in which ethnic minorities are represented. Cross-cultural and cross-national comparative research may offer an interesting perspective on the quality criterion of comparability which can be applied for the assessment of the quality of survey data among ethnic minorities.},
