	abstract = {Summary This chapter describes A System for Product Improvement, Review, and Evaluation (ASPIRE) and discusses the application of ASPIRE to registers and the National Accounts (NA) in Statistics Sweden. It also discusses innovative sensitivity analysis work designed to better understand the impacts of different sources of error on the accuracy of the NA. ASPIRE provides a comprehensive framework for systematically evaluating all dimensions of quality with the primary focus in practice being accuracy. ASPIRE is a system for assessing risks to Accuracy of all processes that produce the key statistics or data elements from a product. It does this by decomposing the total error into major components or error sources and then applying a set of criteria and rating guidelines to evaluate the risk to Accuracy posed by each error source. The chapter presents a case study on quarterly Swedish gross domestic product (GDP) will serve to illustrate the application of ASPIRE to NA.},
