	abstract = {Summary There are a number of ways that Internet-enabled smartphones can affect survey data collection, and the implications of these for various sources of errors are only now being fully explored. There are three broad approaches to the opportunities and challenges posed by mobile Web. The first approach focuses on the many opportunities that such devices can bring to extend and enhance measurement. A second approach to the use of mobile Web relates to the sampling opportunities it may provide. A third approach to mobile Web focuses on respondents who complete Web surveys using mobile devices, whether of their own volition or by design. This chapter focuses on the coverage and nonresponse implications of including or excluding mobile Web users, and the measurement error implications of Web survey completion on mobile devices. Survey researchers have made great strides in adapting to the technological challenges presented by the increased use of mobile devices.},
